Z||000001||fropuff||01-14-2001||11:33 AM||||I'm going to get a 70 HP shot in the summer.  I asked 1FST2M6 if this was alright, and he said it's very difficult to blow the motor with nitrous. (He called it idiot proof--that's good, 'cause I'm an idiot).  He gave me some more information if you want it, but a 70 shot for a 2.8L 6 should be fine.  I'm getting an NOS kit for my 86 GT.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||01-14-2001||11:34 AM||||By the way, an NOS kit is $499; I'm not sure of the part number.  Sorry.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||01-14-2001||04:53 PM||||How difficult is it to install?  For those that don't know me, I'm very mechanically challenged and there isn't anyone around here who does custom work.  My current ride only has a little over 70k miles on it so hopefully it would be stout enough for a shot of NO2.  Looking at late summer to early fall.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||01-14-2001||06:06 PM||||Well, I'm not sure of the difficulty of installing a kit, but Travis told me that it's pretty easy.  He said it would even be easy for me, with little or no mechanical ability.  I think I'm going to get someone else to install it for me, or at least have someone help.  The directions are supposed to be easy to follow.  I looked on the NOS site, and it said that NOS isn't the best for high mileage engines, but that's probably 100K miles+.  Mine's got 63K on it, and I assume that'll be okay.  70K should be fine as well.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
